# Mobile / LAN preview — keep the phone in sync

Sim often checks UI on a real phone at `http://<Mac-LAN-IP>:3000/...` (not
`localhost` — on the phone that is the phone itself). Desktop HMR does **not**
reliably update Safari on the LAN. Stale CSS/JS is the usual “no change” report.

## After any change Sim will look at on a phone

Do **all** of these before ending the turn (not optional):

1. **Confirm the change is served** — `curl` the relevant URL or CSS chunk
   (prefer the LAN IP if known) and grep for a distinctive class/string you just
   shipped. If it isn’t there, fix or restart before telling Sim it’s done.
2. **Restart the Next.js dev server** when the edit was global CSS
   (`globals.css`), `next.config.*`, middleware, Tailwind config, or when Sim
   already reported the phone didn’t update. Kill whatever is on `:3000`, then
   `npm run dev -- -p 3000` (binds `*:3000`).
3. **Tell Sim the exact URL + refresh** in one short line, e.g.
   `Hard-refresh http://192.168.x.x:3000/<path> (or open a Private tab).`
   Resolve the LAN IP with `ipconfig getifaddr en0` (or `en1`) when needed —
   don’t invent it.
4. **Never assume HMR reached the phone.** Desktop looking correct ≠ phone
   updated.

## Standing habits

- Prefer changes that show up in **HTML class names** or obvious copy (easier
  to verify with `curl`) over pure computed-style tweaks when debugging sync.
- If Sim says “no change” on mobile: restart server → verify with `curl` →
  Private-tab URL. Don’t keep editing blindly.
- `/lab` is the lab hero; `/` is the live home hero — confirm which surface
  they mean before declaring a fix live.
